---
// Part 2 — copy from the 5 Nov Linear tickets (ADA-49 to 54), one 70ch column.
// Each section opens on a full-bleed <Scene>; the photographs were chosen by the
// client (credits in src/assets/story/README.md).
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Scene from '../components/Scene.astro';
import ReadProgress from '../components/ReadProgress.astro';
import gathering from '../assets/story/hope-v2-01-answer-is-us.jpg';
import stands from '../assets/story/hope-v2-02-real-democracy.jpg';
import cliffs from '../assets/story/hope-v2-03-immigration.jpg';
import tea from '../assets/story/hope-v2-04-reconnection.jpg';
import candles from '../assets/story/hope-v2-05-believe-in-us.jpg';
---

<Layout title="Our Real Hope — We The People" introLines={['Our Real', 'Hope']}>
  <PageHero lines={['Our Real', 'Hope']} />

  <ReadProgress />
  <article class="prose">
    <Scene
      first
      eager
      src={gathering}
      alt="A huge crowd of people of all ages filling The Mall under rows of Union flags"
      heading="The answer is us. We The People ourselves."
      credit={{
        name: 'Jonny Gios',
        href: 'https://unsplash.com/@supergios?utm_source=unsplash&utm_medium=referral&utm_content=creditCopyText',
        source: 'Unsplash',
        sourceHref:
          'https://unsplash.com/photos/a-large-group-of-people-are-gathered-together-8iq0yqemBuU?utm_source=unsplash&utm_medium=referral&utm_content=creditCopyText',
      }}
    />
    <p>
      It’s our right to make the big decisions shaping our lives and our country, not
      compromised politicians with their own agendas.
    </p>
    <p>
      And when everyday people take the lead, something powerful happens: common sense
      returns. Both practical wisdom and the understanding that there are values that we
      share.
    </p>
    <p>
      We realise that, given the chance, ordinary people are capable of more nuanced
      conversations than the politicians that claim to represent us.
    </p>
    <p>
      We learn to trust each other again. That means we make fairer decisions that truly
      reflect who we are.
    </p>

    <Scene
      src={stands}
      alt="A packed stand of people on their feet, many waving Union flags"
      heading="That is the power of real democracy"
    />
    <p>
      But for that to happen, we have to speak openly with each other.<br />
      To <em>really</em> listen to other views, despite the depth of our differences.<br />
      To see the other side as human. To allow them to change our minds.
    </p>
    <p>Maybe we’ve always struggled to do this. But right now it is harder than ever.</p>
    <p>
      We’ve lost our common ground: both the places we used to meet, as well as the
      unspoken agreements that guide our conversation.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>We The People</strong> is about finding our way back. And we believe we need
      to start with the hardest question of all.
    </p>

    <Scene
      src={cliffs}
      alt="Storm waves breaking below the white chalk cliffs of the south coast"
      heading="Immigration"
      focus="40% 50%"
    />
    <p>Immigration has become the fault line tearing Britain apart.</p>
    <p>
      You may think it’s the most important issue of our time, or a distraction from what
      really matters. Either way, nothing else divides us so deeply or so dangerously.
    </p>
    <p>This is the fire to put out first, before it burns the country down.</p>
    <p>
      So from kitchen tables to community halls to a great national gathering,
      <strong>We The People</strong> will help the people of Britain to explore the question:
    </p>
    <p class="pull">What do you think about immigration and how this country might approach it?</p>

    <Scene
      src={tea}
      alt="Two women in silhouette talking over cups of tea at a table by a window"
      heading="Reconnection & Reconciliation"
    />
    <p>
      These conversations may be hard. We’ll hear things we don’t agree with. We might feel
      angry or upset.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>We The People</strong> offers ways to help make it happen without descending
      into an argument.
    </p>
    <p>
      From our <a href="/be-part-of-it#you">#AgreeOnTea campaign</a>, which gives you
      everything you need for a one-to-one conversation over a cuppa, to hands-on
      facilitation for larger gatherings we call
      <a href="/be-part-of-it#community">Councils of the People</a>.
    </p>
    <p>Our ground rules and structures change everything.</p>
    <p>
      Instead of shouting over each other, they create the chance for connection, founded on
      a simple principle that sits at the heart of our movement: to be heard, we have to be
      willing to listen.
    </p>
    <p>And we might be surprised by what we discover.</p>
    <p>
      An agreed diagnosis of what’s gone wrong. A story that strikes a chord beyond the
      noise. A shared fear for the future, despite our different values.
    </p>
    <p>
      Perhaps a recognition that we all care for our country, even if we have different
      visions for what it needs.
    </p>
    <p>We might realise that we aren’t monsters or enemies but fellow human beings.</p>

    <Scene
      src={candles}
      alt="A crowd at night, each person holding up a lit candle"
      heading="We start to believe in “us” again"
    />
    <p>
      We believe that beyond the stories of our divisions, we may actually be more united
      than we’re led to believe.
    </p>
    <p>
      Even now, 70% of us still say we trust people in general (ONS 2026). Covid-19 showed
      us that despite our differences we could still come together and support each other in
      a crisis. It’s not just wishful thinking.
    </p>
    <p>
      A fresh collective approach to our problems is possible, if only we are given the
      chance.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is how we reclaim our power, and our right to make the decisions that shape our
      lives, starting with immigration.
    </p>
    <p>
      At the peak of our movement, <strong>We The People</strong> will bring the whole
      country together at a
      <a href="/be-part-of-it#country">National Council of the People on Immigration</a>,
      to forge the first approach to this issue written by us, the people, not politicians.
      A policy in all our names, that we can all accept.
    </p>
    <p>
      This will be a demonstration of a powerful new way to do democracy, inspired by the
      latest political theory as well as deep democratic tradition (find out more on our
      <a href="/foundations">Foundations page</a>).
    </p>
    <p>
      One better equipped for the complex challenges we face. One where we take the lead.
    </p>

    <p class="pull">This is how we turn things around.</p>

    <a class="back" href="/be-part-of-it">Be Part of It →</a>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    var back = document.querySelector('article.prose .back');
    if (!back) return;
    var fired = false;
    var observer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      entries.forEach(function (entry) {
        if (entry.isIntersecting && !fired) {
          fired = true;
          window.posthog?.capture('hope_article_read');
          observer.disconnect();
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.5 });
    observer.observe(back);
  });
</script>
